XR window: what comes out of it stays within a half cylinder, not a pyramid

WakerQuest 1.2.2. What came out of the window was cut by the rectangle narrowing toward the game camera's
eye, which left little of it to see. It now ends on a half cylinder standing on the window, its axis upright
through the window's middle: the window's width across, the pop-out's depth toward the player (round when
that is half the width, else an ellipse), the window's height.

- The eyes' mask (stereo.cpp, patch 0030): the half cylinder's round side fades over window_fade, but never at
  the window's plane, so nothing goes see-through where the picture meets it.
- The GX shader's discard (patch 0037): the same volume. The command's f32 is now how far it comes out, not
  the camera's depth.
- The eye scissor (patch 0033): the rectangle's corners and the half cylinder's arcs, every 30 degrees.

